	Disable Manjaro's custom prompt and use your own

	If you want full control over your prompt:

 	Open your .zshrc:

		nano ~/.zshrc

    	Comment out these lines to stop loading Manjaro's prompt:

		# source /usr/share/zsh/manjaro-zsh-config
		# source /usr/share/zsh/manjaro-zsh-prompt

    	Add your custom prompt, for example:

		PROMPT='%F{blue}%1~%f %# '
           or
                PROMPT='%1~$ '  //change ~ %  to ~$

   	Reload Zsh:

		exec zsh